en  many more households are given  accommodation in a different local  Authority but still in the same region  like mabinty in 2018 to 19 8.8 percent  of placements were in a different local  Authority last year that went up to 11.6  percent  and campaigners warn the problem is only  likely to get worse it's almost like a  perfect storm so you know we had a  pre-existing housing emergency we've  been going backwards in terms of  delivery of social homes for years  people are being hit by the cost of  living crisis and of course that means  that people are even less likely to be  able to afford their rent mabinty and  her children were already caught in that  storm tossed from one Council to another  the clouds could be gathering for many  more Tom Cheshire Sky News South London
 

